00:00:38.360 --> 00:00:40.564
Let's first answer what
Pub/Sub means as a service.

00:00:40.564 --> 00:00:41.480
PRIYANKA VERGADIA: OK.

00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:43.520
So a published
subscribed service

00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:46.760
is a messaging service where
the senders of messages, called

00:00:46.760 --> 00:00:50.360
publishers, are decoupled
from receivers of messages,

00:00:50.360 --> 00:00:51.219
called subscribers.

00:00:51.219 --> 00:00:52.760
HEATHER CROSS: The
published messages

00:00:52.760 --> 00:00:54.500
are categorized into topics.

00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:56.600
Subscribers who have
expressed interest in a topic

00:00:56.600 --> 00:00:58.400
will either pull
related messages

00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:00.904
or choose to get push
messages from the topic.

00:01:00.904 --> 00:01:02.570
Key to the service
is that neither party

00:01:02.570 --> 00:01:04.528
is required to have any
knowledge of the other.

00:01:09.322 --> 00:01:10.780
PRIYANKA VERGADIA:
Cloud Pub/Sub is

00:01:10.780 --> 00:01:13.420
great for distributing
event notifications.

00:01:13.420 --> 00:01:16.660
Take an example of a service
that accepts user sign-ups.

00:01:16.660 --> 00:01:20.170
It can send notifications
whenever a new user registers,

00:01:20.170 --> 00:01:22.300
and downstream
services can subscribe

00:01:22.300 --> 00:01:25.180
to receive notifications
of that event.

00:01:25.180 --> 00:01:27.620
There are even examples
closer to home.

00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:29.950
You know that smart home
technology you're so fond of?

00:01:29.950 --> 00:01:31.610
HEATHER CROSS: Yes, I
do love my Google Home.

00:01:31.610 --> 00:01:32.940
PRIYANKA VERGADIA: Well,
the Pub/Sub service

00:01:32.940 --> 00:01:34.630
is a part of the
architecture that

00:01:34.630 --> 00:01:37.450
supports the streaming of
data from residential sensors

00:01:37.450 --> 00:01:39.559
to the backend servers
that are hosted on cloud.

00:01:39.559 --> 00:01:41.350
HEATHER CROSS: The
ability of Cloud Pub/Sub

00:01:41.350 --> 00:01:43.600
to ingest millions of
streaming events per second

00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:46.840
from anywhere in the world also
allows you to respond to events

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:47.980
as they happen.

00:01:47.980 --> 00:01:51.070
Cloud Pub/Sub forms part
of Cloud's Stream Analytics

00:01:51.070 --> 00:01:53.770
solution, which provides a
number of useful applications

00:01:53.770 --> 00:01:56.020
such as performing
sentiment analysis,

00:01:56.020 --> 00:01:58.540
identifying general
patterns and trends in data,

00:01:58.540 --> 00:02:00.910
monitoring the performance
and reach of campaigns,

00:02:00.910 --> 00:02:02.800
and crafting messages
in real time.

